# Walkthrough: Math Rendering & Navigation Fixes

I have resolved the rendering issues and usability hurdles in both the Document and Presentation views.

## 🛠️ Key Improvements

### 🧪 Robust Math Parsing
The custom tag system (`{{id:content}}`) is now much more resilient.
- **Nested Braces Support**: The parser previously failed on matrices (e.g., `\begin{bmatrix} ... \end{bmatrix}`) because of the internal `}`. It now correctly identifies the final `}}` closure.
- **Color Resolution**: KaTeX's `\color` command does not natively support CSS variables like `var(--teal)`. I've added a resolver that maps these variable names to their hexadecimal counterparts before they reach the rendering engine, eliminating the "red text" parse errors.

### 🧭 Sticky UI & Navigation
- **Persistent Header**: The header in the Document view is now `position: sticky`. Whether you are at Step 1 or Step 11, the **Presentation** and **Document** toggle buttons will remain at the top of your screen.
- **High Visibility**: Increased the `z-index` and added a backdrop-blur effect to ensure the navigation bar stays on top of all math and canvas elements.

### 📚 Content Polish
- **Typo Fix**: Corrected "Grame-Schmidt" to "Gram-Schmidt" in the lesson narration.
- **Sync**: Verified that all 11 steps of the Gram-Schmidt derivation now render perfectly in the scrolled document view as well as the animated presentation view.

## 🎬 Verification Result

> [!TIP]
> You can now see the "Presentation" button at the top of the Document view. Clicking it will transition you into the fluid, video-like animation mode we built.

